# Keep the random seed on the writable partition.
#
# seedrng defaults to /var/lib/seedrng, which is on the read-only root, so it has
# nowhere to write. Pointing it at a tmpfs would make the error go away without
# making the seed persist -- which is what an earlier revision of this board did by
# mounting a tmpfs on /var, and the giveaway was in the boot log every time:
# "Saving 256 bits of non-creditable seed for next boot". Non-creditable, because
# the directory was empty again on each boot. The seed only earns entropy credit if
# it is still there next time.
#
# S01seedrng runs long before S15bootpart has mounted anything, so on that first
# call this directory does not exist and seedrng fails -- harmlessly, the init
# script ends in `|| true`. S15bootpart reloads it once the partition is up, which
# is the refresh the script's own header describes, and that is the call that
# counts.
#
# See /etc/zlyme.conf for where this is and why.

. /etc/zlyme.conf

SEEDRNG_ARGS="--seed-dir=${ZLYME_CFG}/seedrng"
